      "content": "Neither framework alone is likely to provide a stable long-term solution; instead, comprehensive success typically requires a hybrid approach that combines rigorous border security with robust immigration pathways. Research consistently indicates that increasing unauthorized immigration costs significantly more in public services and lost productivity than the estimated savings from enhanced enforcement, while pathways to citizenship tend to boost economic growth and stabilize communities. Therefore, the most effective strategy may involve integrating strict legal enforcement at the border alongside expanded, merit- and humanitarian-based routes to legal status.",
